# SVG Animation System

This project uses a custom SVG animation system built with SVG.js. The main components are:

## Core Components

- [app/scripts/svgjs-anim.js](mdc:app/scripts/svgjs-anim.js) - Main animation controller class that manages the SVG scene and animations
- [app/scripts/svg-extensions.js](mdc:app/scripts/svg-extensions.js) - Contains all SVG element extensions (Step, Skip, Elevator, etc.)

## Dependencies

The system relies on these key npm packages:
- @svgdotjs/svg.js - Core SVG manipulation library
- eventbusjs - Event handling system
- modernizr - Feature detection
- classie - Class manipulation utilities

## Animation Elements

The system includes several animated elements, each defined as an SVG extension:
- Step - Basic step animation
- Skip - Skip animation
- Elevator - Elevator movement
- DumpTruck - Dump truck operations
- Scooptram - Scooptram movement
- ITHDrill - In-the-hole drilling
- GroundSupport - Ground support operations
- JumboDrill - Jumbo drilling
- Longholes - Longhole drilling
- RockBreaker - Rock breaking operations
- JawCrusher - Jaw crusher operations
- Zimba - Zimba operations
- Zoom - Zoom functionality

## Usage

The animation system is initialized in [app/index.html](mdc:app/index.html) and uses ES modules for importing dependencies. Each animation element is created using the SVG.invent() method and can be controlled through the SVGjsAnim class.

## Event System

The system uses EventBus for communication between components:
- clicked_heading - Triggered when a heading is clicked
- clicked_Scene - Triggered when the scene is clicked
- play_video - Triggered to play a video
- stop_video - Triggered to stop video playback
